//? Title: Binary long division
//? Subtitle: Actual64-bit execution, exact prefix invariants and the original arithmetic examples
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Binary long division brings down one input bit, compares the trial remainder
with the divisor, and optionally subtracts. This report retains the original
examples while capturing the native fixed64-step execution instead of replacing
it with a separate significant-bit demonstration.
)

\toc

> Shift, compare, subtract

At each real step, bring down the next dividend bit into the remainder. If the
trial remainder is at least the nonzero divisor, subtract once and set that
quotient bit. After processing a prefix P, its partial quotient Q and remainder
R satisfy P=Q*D+R and0<=R<D. The returned full quotient stores set bits in their
original positions throughout; shifting that partial stored quotient right by
the current bit position yields Q for this invariant.

For220/13, the returned quotient is16 and remainder12. The native loop processes
bits63 through0, including leading zeros: it always performs64 comparisons. The
selected transition diagram below comes directly from an actual captured step
that subtracts.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/long_division_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/long_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::long_division_trace(220, 13);
    auto it = std::find_if(t.steps.begin(), t.steps.end(), [](auto &s) {
        return s.subtracted;
    });
    auto &s = *it;
    std::print("Actual quotient {}; remainder {}; actual processed bits {}; first actual subtraction at bit " "{}.\n",
               t.result.quotient, t.result.remainder, t.result.iterations, s.bit);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("before", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual prior remainder\n{}", s.before)).node("trial", {6, 0}, std::format("Actual brought-down trial\n{} >= divisor {}", s.trial, t.divisor)).node("after", {12, 0}, std::format("Actual committed remainder\n{}", s.remainder)).edge("before", "trial").edge("trial", "after");
    d.save_svg("build/long_division_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Actual quotient 16; remainder 12; actual processed bits 64; first actual subtraction at bit 4.
\image(figures/long_division_tiny.svg)
// result_end
