> Original examples and exact outputs

The original100/7,220/13,1000000/999 and42/42 examples are retained. The figure
compares their returned remainders with divisors; every remainder must be below
its divisor. Different magnitudes are shown numerically in the computed table,
not interpreted as comparable difficulty: each call executes the same64-step
loop.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/long_division_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/long_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| dividend | divisor | actual quotient | actual remainder | actual iterations |\n| ---: | " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    int i = 0;
    for (auto[n, d] : std::vector<std::pair<std::uint64_t, std::uint64_t>>{
         {100, 7}, {220, 13}, {1000000, 999}, {42, 42}
     }) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::long_division_trace(n, d);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n, d, t.result.quotient,
                   t.result.remainder, t.result.iterations);
        x.push_back(i++);
        y.push_back(double(t.result.remainder) / d);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual remainder/divisor", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(
        0, 1.1).x_label("original example index").y_label(
        "actual remainder divided by divisor").title("Original exact divisions: remainders below divisors").save_svg("build/long_division_original.svg");
}
```
