> Full-width safety and invalid divisors

Although a trial remainder is shifted, this fixed-width algorithm does not need
a65-bit remainder register. Before each step the processed input prefix contains
at most63 bits; its remainder is no larger than that prefix. Bringing down one
bit therefore fits uint64 exactly. After comparison/subtraction the remainder is
again below the divisor. This proof depends on processing a single64-bit
dividend; it should not be generalized to arbitrarily long streams with the same
register.

A zero divisor now throws invalid_argument before any division steps. The
previous implementation lacked that guard. A trace quota counts two input words
plus64 actual records, so a nonzero cap below66 throws before capture; zero
disables the optional cap. It counts logical records, not fields, capacities or
bytes. Ordinary execution has constant auxiliary storage; the fixed-width trace
owns64 records and does not replay execution. No external dataset is relevant to
exact unsigned arithmetic.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/long_division_width.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/long_division.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/plot.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <print>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto m = std::numeric_limits<std::uint64_t>::max();
    std::vector<double> x, y;
    std::print("| full-width dividend | divisor | actual quotient | actual remainder | actual comparisons " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    int k = 0;
    for (std::uint64_t d : {std::uint64_t{1}, m, m - 1, std::uint64_t{1} << 63}) {
        auto t = dm::algorithms::long_division_trace(m, d);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", m, d, t.result.quotient,
                   t.result.remainder, t.result.iterations);
        x.push_back(k++);
        y.push_back(t.steps.size());
    }
    bool rejected = false;
    try {
        auto r = dm::algorithms::long_division(1, 0);
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        rejected = true;
    }
    std::print("\nActual zero-divisor rejection {}.\n", rejected);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual processed bits", {37, 99, 235}, 6).y_limits(0, 75).x_label("full-width divisor control index").y_label("actual native bit steps").title("Fixed64-step cost across full-width controls").save_svg("build/long_division_width.svg");
}
```
